    "answer": {
      "short": "862 shoes.",
      "worked": "Pairs owned by the first group:\n$$\\begin{array}{rrr}&2&5\\\\\\times&&7\\\\\\hline 1&7&5\\end{array}$$\nPairs owned by the second group:\n$$\\begin{array}{rrr}&3&2\\\\\\times&&8\\\\\\hline 2&5&6\\end{array}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Total pairs}&=175+256\\\\\\text{Total pairs}&=431\\\\\\text{Total shoes}&=431\\times2\\\\\\text{Total shoes}&=862\\end{align*}$$\nEach pair contains 2 shoes, so the 57 people own 862 shoes.",
